<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>(a) A posho mill grinds <m>{560}</m> kg of maize in <m>{4}</m> hours. Working at the same rate, how long does it take to grind <m>{980}</m> kg?</p><p><fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/> hours  </p><p>(b) <m>{15}</m> workers can weed a shamba in <m>{8}</m> days. How many days would <m>{12}</m> workers take, working at the same rate?</p><p><fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> days  </p><p>Give each answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) More maize takes more time: this is direct proportion, so the ratio of time to mass stays the same.</p><p><m>{560}</m> kg take <m>{4}</m> hours.<br/>1 kg takes <m>\dfrac{ {4} }{ {560} }</m> hours.<br/><m>{980}</m> kg take <m>\dfrac{ {4} }{ {560} } \times {980} = {7}</m> hours.</p><p>(b) More workers finish sooner: this is inverse proportion, so the product of workers and days stays the same.</p><p><m>{15}</m> workers take <m>{8}</m> days.<br/>1 worker takes <m>{15} \times {8} = {120}</m> days.<br/><m>{12}</m> workers take <m>{120} \div {12} = {10}</m> days.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>7</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>10</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>